{
  "esm": "2.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_cgrid_grad_x",
    "description": "The zonal C-grid kinetic-energy-gradient rewrite target D(KE, wrt: x) on the mom6_cgrid: lowers the spatial derivative of the cell kinetic energy KE [i,j,k] to the east-face zonal gradient KEx(i,j,k) = (KE(i+1,j,k) - KE(i,j,k)) * IdxCu(i,j) (the KE_ARAKAWA gradient term -d(KE)/dx of the Coriolis + momentum-advection acceleration, MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 gradKE :1249-1397 with the face difference (KE(i+1,j) - KE(i,j))*G%IdxCu(I,j) of the KEx loop :1300-1320; IdxCu(i,j) = 1/dxCu is the east-face 1/length so the gradient lives on the east faces). SOLID-WALL BOUNDARY: the east face at the domain edge (i = N_I) is a wall whose normal kinetic-energy gradient is identically zero, so the i = N_I region is the EXPLICIT free-slip wall value KEx(N_I,j,k) = 0 — NOT the clamped difference (KE(N_I) - KE(N_I))*IdxCu = 0 of a naive halo closure (the clamped form happens to evaluate to zero here, but it hides the wall as if the cell duplicated; this rule states the wall explicitly). The rule is a GROUND per-variable selector (esm-spec 9.6.1): KE is NOT a parameter, so the match arg \"KE\" is a literal that fires only on the derivative of the declared variable named KE, with priority 20 to outrank the wildcard mom6_cgrid_div_x (priority 10) when both are imported. SHAPE GUARD: esm-spec 9.6.1 admits `where` keys only for declared params (a non-param key is apply_expression_template_invalid_declaration), so a ground selector cannot carry a where shape constraint; making KE a param to constrain it would turn the rule into a wildcard D(*, x) over [i,j,k] fields that outranks mom6_cgrid_div_x on every operand. The guard is therefore the literal name: the rule fires only on D(KE, x) of a variable named KE, and a consumer importing it must declare KE as the [i,j,k] field this rule assumes (the momentum fixtures and problems/mom6_cgrid_momentum.esm do). Unlike the vort rules, D(KE, x) IS a derivative: the face difference is scaled by IdxCu (KEx of gradKE, MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90:1404). KE and IdxCu are free names resolved in the consuming model (the free-name contract of grids/mom6_cgrid/grid.esm); the body's KE is the matched operand.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:mom6_cgrid",
      "grid:mom6_cgrid",
      "op:grad",
      "order:1",
      "bc:wall",
      "axes:i,j,k",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
      },
      {
        "citation": "MOM6 source: MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc gradKE :1249-1397, KEx at :1300-1320; the east-face convention of the mom6_cgrid grid.esm."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "mom6_cgrid_grad_x": {
      "params": [],
      "priority": 20,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": ["KE"],
        "wrt": "x"
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [
            [1, { "op": "-", "args": ["N_I", 1] }],
            [1, "N_J"],
            [1, "N_K"]
          ],
          [
            ["N_I", "N_I"],
            [1, "N_J"],
            [1, "N_K"]
          ]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j", "k"],
            "args": ["KE", "IdxCu"],
            "ranges": {
              "i": [1, { "op": "-", "args": ["N_I", 1] }],
              "j": [1, "N_J"],
              "k": [1, "N_K"]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["IdxCu", "i", "j"]
                },
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": ["KE", { "op": "+", "args": ["i", 1] }, "j", "k"]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": ["KE", "i", "j", "k"]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          0.0
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
